{"tool_name":"qualimap","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","debian","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"qualimap","version":"2.3","home":"http://qualimap.bioinfo.cipf.es/","license":"GPL-2.0-or-later","summary":"Quality control of alignment sequencing data and its derivatives like feature counts","identifiers":["biotools:qualimap"],"license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"noarch":"generic","number":0,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"run":["fonts-conda-ecosystem","openjdk","bioconductor-noiseq","r-optparse","r-xml","bioconductor-rsamtools","bioconductor-rtracklayer"]},"source_url":"https://bitbucket.org/kokonech/qualimap/downloads/qualimap_v2.3.zip","test":{"commands":["qualimap --java-mem-size=250M -h"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"qualimap","identifiers":["biotools:qualimap","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/bts503"],"license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"Platform-independent application written in java and r that provides both a graphical user inteface (gui) and a command-line interface to facilitate the quality control of alignment sequencing data.","home_url":"https://bitbucket.org/kokonech/qualimap/src/master/","keywords":["Genomics","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Quality Control","Sequence Alignment","Data quality management"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":3627},"biotools":{"id":"qualimap","home":"https://qualimap.bioinfo.cipf.es/","summary":"Platform-independent application written in Java and R that provides both a Graphical User Inteface (GUI) and a command-line interface to facilitate the quality control of alignment sequencing data.","addition_date":"2017-01-13T13:16:00Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:34:14.875362Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:qualimap","credit":[{"name":"QualiMap Forum","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/qualimap"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://qualimap.bioinfo.cipf.es/doc_html/index.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-CZ"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequencing quality control","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3218"}]}],"name":"QualiMap","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"seqwiki_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bts503","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: The sequence alignment/map (SAM) and the binary alignment/map (BAM) formats have become the standard method of representation of nucleotide sequence alignments for next-generation sequencing data. SAM/BAM files usually contain information from tens to hundreds of millions of reads. Often, the sequencing technology, protocol and/or the selected mapping algorithm introduce some unwanted biases in these data. The systematic detection of such biases is a non-trivial task that is crucial to drive appropriate downstream analyses.Results: We have developed Qualimap, a Java application that supports user-friendly quality control of mapping data, by considering sequence features and their genomic properties. Qualimap takes sequence alignment data and provides graphical and statistical analyses for the evaluation of data. Such quality-control data are vital for highlighting problems in the sequencing and/or mapping processes, which must be addressed prior to further analyses. \u00a9 The Author 2012. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Carbonell J."},{"name":"Conesa A."},{"name":"Cruz L.M."},{"name":"Dopazo J."},{"name":"Garcia-Alcalde F."},{"name":"Gotz S."},{"name":"Meyer T.F."},{"name":"Okonechnikov K."},{"name":"Tarazona S."}],"citationCount":675,"date":"2012-10-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Qualimap: Evaluating next-generation sequencing alignment data"},"pmid":"22914218"}],"topic":[{"term":"Data quality management","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3572"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"QualiMap","home":"https://bio.tools/qualimap","summary":"Platform-independent application written in Java and R that provides both a Graphical User Inteface (GUI) and a command-line interface to facilitate the quality control of alignment sequencing data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"2.3","first_commit":"2019-10-10","conda_name":"qualimap","conda_version":"2.3","summary":"Qualimap 2 is a platform-independent application written in Java andR that facilitates the quality control of alignment sequencing data and itsderivatives like feature counts.","edam_operations":["Sequencing quality control"],"edam_topics":["Data quality management"],"toolshed_categories":["Sequence Analysis","Transcriptomics","SAM"],"toolshed_id":"qualimap","users_5_years":7452,"users_all_time":7934,"usage_5_years":896155,"usage_all_time":909530,"bio_tools_summary":"Platform-independent application written in Java and R that provides both a Graphical User Inteface (GUI) and a command-line interface to facilitate the quality control of alignment sequencing data.","bio_tools_ids":"qualimap","bio_tools_name":"QualiMap","related_tutorials":["https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/variant-analysis/tutorials/aiv-analysis/tutorial.html","https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/variant-analysis/tutorials/pox-tiled-amplicon/tutorial.html","https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/variant-analysis/tutorials/tb-variant-analysis/tutorial.html"],"related_workflows":[{"create_time":"2026-01-12","latest_version":"2","link":"https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1647?version=2","name":"TB Variant Analysis v1.0"},{"create_time":"2026-07-15","latest_version":"5","link":"https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2027?version=5","name":"host-contamination-removal-long-reads/main"},{"create_time":"2026-03-10","latest_version":"7","link":"https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/155?version=7","name":"sars-cov-2-pe-illumina-artic-ivar-analysis/SARS-COV-2-ILLUMINA-AMPLICON-IVAR-PA